{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-13T20:29:33.477Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7ed53804faba291cc8b1a6ce","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1460","claim:pm-gh1461","lineage:pm-gh1461","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1460+pm-gh1461","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1460","claim:pm-gh1461","lineage:pm-gh1461","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1462\n\n## Problem\nExtension packages render through the host, so TOON is their default output, and their acceptance tests need to assert on what the host actually printed. The public SDK (`@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk`, `/sdk/testing`, `/sdk/core`, …) exposes no TOON decoder: there is no `decodeToon`, `parseToon` or equivalent. Authors fall back to one of three bad options:\n1. **Hard-coding quoting**, as in `assert.match(out, /status: \"open\"/)`. This broke when the host renderer started emitting unquoted scalars (unbraind/pm-github#115 CI went red after a toolchain bump).\n2. **Deep-importing internals**: `import { decodeToonItemContent } from \"@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/core/item/toon-decode.js\"`. This sits outside the exports map and can break on any release.\n3. **Adding `@toon-format/toon` as a devDependency pinned to whatever pm-cli uses internally (4.1.1 today).** That duplicates the pin, and any skew means the test parser disagrees with the host renderer.\n\n## Proposal\n- Export `decodeToon(text)` (and ideally `encodeToon(value)`) from `@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/testing`, or from `/sdk`, backed by exactly the TOON implementation the host renders with.\n- In the authoring docs, recommend asserting host output as `decodeToon(stdout)` rather than by string matching.\n- Optional: `createExtensionTestHarness` gives a `run(...)` result exposing `.parsed` for both `--json` and TOON output.\n\nThat makes extension tests independent of quoting and whitespace changes in the renderer, and removes a reason to reach into `dist/`.\n\n\nImplementation intent\n\nExpose a typed public SDK testing codec over the same pinned TOON implementation used by the host renderer, enabling semantic output assertions without deep imports or duplicated package dependencies."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1462"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1462: Publish host-aligned TOON codecs for extension acceptance tests"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Expose a typed public SDK testing codec over the same pinned TOON implementation used by the host renderer, enabling semantic output assertions without deep imports or duplicated package dependencies."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:extensions","area:sdk","github-intake","output","testing","toon"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-13T20:29:33.477Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-13T20:29:33.477Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Public exports decode real host-rendered output semantically; Support encoded and decoded JSON values without quoting assertions; Prove installed/public Node and Bun consumers and TypeScript types; Document the canonical package-author workflow"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Installed package authors parse host-rendered TOON through public SDK exports and round-trip supported JSON values with the host codec, with documented assertions and no extra runtime dependency."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-jcyn","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:29:33.477Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ko35zx","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:29:33.477Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-13T20:29:33.477Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"{\"text\":\"Duplicate check: complete live2956-item all-status corpus with zero omissions and unreadable records, request-specific searches and open/in-progress inventories. Full live closed predecessors pm-jcyn and pm-ko35zx describe shipped adjacent contracts, not this new reported scope. Reuse pm-ugqx parent lineage and relate predecessors without reopening completed work. Full GitHub issue and comments read. Official Git documentation distinguishes -merge binary conflict behavior from the native text/default drivers. Implementation will preserve supported SDK contracts and use real controls.\"}"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"249afb2a13db08ac7e19c406a9aff8f527924212991e8b9e9bfb2b19f48992a0","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_